I've added a rule that displays information under each pin thumbnail in the grid. Here's what you'll now see below each pin:

1. **Description** — The alt text/description of the image (e.g., "a cat is sitting on the toilet looking at the camera with an odd look to it's face"), shown in a readable 2-line truncated format.

2. **Source reference** — A line showing the image domain and pin ID (e.g., "📌 i.pinimg.com/pin/238127899043301037"), so you can identify where the image comes from.

The info is displayed in a subtle style with a light border separator, keeping it unobtrusive while giving you context before clicking any pin.

**Note:** Pinterest doesn't expose the original website domain (the site the pin was saved from) in the DOM for logged-out users — only the image CDN URL (`i.pinimg.com`) is available. If you log in, Pinterest may load additional metadata like the source domain and full pin description, which could be enhanced further.

